    "stdout": "12bf89d56459b084c60f9add7739fe0ea0be4477\n12bf89d56459b084c60f9add7739fe0ea0be4477\ntag v2.3.0\nTagger: pi-action-agent[bot] <355532786+pi-action-agent[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\n\nv2.3.0\n12bf89d56459b084c60f9add7739fe0ea0be4477 chore: release 2.3.0 (#45)\n{\"body\":\"\\n### Added\\n- **Working-tree continuity** (#33, added in #44). A thread now keeps the files that pi leaves uncommitted, staged and unstaged, on `refs/pi/worktrees/<number>`, and restores them at the start of the next run. When you rewind or fork the conversation, the files rewind too. Two new inputs: `worktree_snapshots` (default `true`) and `worktree_snapshot_exclude`. See [Working-tree continuity](https://github.com/cv/pi-action/blob/v2.3.0/docs/threads.md#working-tree-continuity).\\n- **A workflow log that shows what pi does** (#46, added in #48, #49, and #50). The log shows one line for each step while pi works: `💬` for the text of the model, `🔧` when a tool call starts, and `↳ ✓` or `↳ ✗ failed` when it ends. Click a `↳` line to see the arguments of the call and the last 30 lines of its output. Each reply gets a `✅ Replied` line with the comment and totals: model responses, tool calls, time, and tokens. The setup is in a collapsed `Setup` group. The thread, with the git commands that read it, is now at the start of the log. Pushes and working-tree snapshots are debug messages: to see them, enable step debug logging. See [The workflow log](https://github.com/cv/pi-action/blob/v2.3.0/docs/how-it-works.md#the-workflow-log).\\n\\n### Fixed\\n- **A fetch by pi no longer breaks the run** (#46, fixed in #47). If pi fetched into `refs/pi/*`, for example with `git fetch origin '+refs/pi/*:refs/pi/*'`, it moved the ref that the run was writing to. The session then failed without a reply, a reaction, or a failed step. A run now keeps its refs on `refs/pi-action/*` on the runner, and pushes them to `refs/pi/*` on the remote. See [Protection against conflicts](https://github.com/cv/pi-action/blob/v2.3.0/docs/threads.md#protection-against-conflicts).\\n- **A failed session is reported** (#46, fixed in #47). If the storage of the thread fails, pi-action posts a `❌ pi Error` comment with the cause, adds 😕 to the request, and fails the step.\\n- **No false warning from `Save pi thread state`** (#46, fixed in #47). If the remote already has the local commits, the step writes `already saved` to the log, not a warning.\\n\\n\\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/cv/pi-action/compare/v2.2.2...v2.3.0\\n\",\"isDraft\":true,\"name\":\"v2.3.0\",\"tagName\":\"v2.3.0\",\"targetCommitish\":\"main\"}\ncommit 12bf89d56459b084c60f9add7739fe0ea0be4477\nAuthor: pi-action-agent[bot] <355532786+pi-action-agent[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nDate:   Thu Nov 12 09:35:48 2026 +0000\n\n    chore: release 2.3.0 (#45)\n\n .github/workflows/release.yml | 87 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n CONTRIBUTING.md               | 46 +++++++++++++++++++++--\n package-lock.json             |  4 +-\n package.json                  |  2 +-\n 4 files changed, 132 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)\n3:\t\"version\": \"2.3.0\",\n",
